# package-lock.json is COMMITTED on purpose — do not add it back here.
# Without it, CI's `npm install` re-resolves every caret range from the registry on every build, so a
# dependency compromised between two builds ships in the next installer with nothing in the diff to show
# it. electron-builder alone pulls the got/keyv/cacheable-request chain that the Shai-Hulud npm worm
# targeted (keyv 6.0.0 was published and unpublished inside one day, 2026-08-04). The lock pins exact
# versions AND integrity hashes, and CI uses `npm ci`, which installs the lock verbatim and fails rather
# than silently resolving something newer.
